# Oldest supported dependency set. One "module version" per line; "go" sets the
# language directive. ./test.sh -F rebuilds and retests against these in a
# throwaway copy, so the working tree keeps the versions it ships with.
go 1.22
golang.org/x/crypto v0.31.0
golang.org/x/sys v0.28.0
golang.org/x/term v0.27.0
github.com/sirikothe/gotextfsm v1.1.0
github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0
github.com/gosnmp/gosnmp v1.41.0
github.com/zalando/go-keyring v0.2.8
